In Nethack the wrest-last-wish is no problem, because you have a
sufficient amount of wishes [from that wand] available. The wrest
(mostly WRT but not restricted to wishing) is helpful in Vanilla for
desperate cases where you've been stuck. It's acceptable for such
corner cases to require tedious actions; after all you shall not
be invited to use it as some standard means of problem solution.
If in UnNethack the 0-charge-non-recharable-wand is the most likely
object you will find, it's actually supporting the wishless conduct,
and wishes [from that wand] only designed to help in those desperate
cases. I want to conclude that even if I often inadvertently played
wishless, I think it's not a nicely designed feature in UnNethack.
Patric, if you think that there's too many wishes, just drop the
"wrest-feature" and give that wand a single charge, or drop the wrest
success probability to 10% (instead of less than 1%). I'd leave it
anyway as it's implemented in Vanilla; it's the most sensible, IMO.
(Mind, you've advanced to and cleared the Castle to get that wand.
Is it that bad to wish for some items to reduce boredom or get
some helpful item that the stingy RNG refused to create randomly?
Refrain from wishing for a magic whistle? Refrain from wishing for
the missing seven candles?)

